<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helsingborg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helsingborg is a port city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, on the narrowest point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">Øresund</a> opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helsingor">Helsingør</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. Danish for most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, its castle guarded the Sound, and in 1362 Valdemar IV defeated a Hanseatic fleet off the town. It passed to Sweden in 1658, and in 1710 a Swedish army under Magnus Stenbock defeated a Danish invasion force at the Battle of Helsingborg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helsingborg.jpg" alt="Helsingborg" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This image was produced by me, David Castor (dcastor). The pictures I submit to the Wikipedia Project are released to the public domain. … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inre_hamnen_i_Helsingborg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
